{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter's Dating Misadventures", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "I Just Can't Get It Right", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Expressing Understanding Using Modals ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty.<br /> You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to describe degrees of certainty.<br /> You can use modals with the Present Perfect to talk about the possibility of a past event that is not clear in the present context.<br /> Example:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">must have</span> been quite upset about that.</span> <br /><br /> Must = it's very likely <br /> Must not / Could not / Can't = it's not possible<br /> May / Might / Can / Could = it's possible<br /> May not / Might not = it's possible this is not true", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Modal </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Meaning </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> There must be something you can do! </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's very likely there is something you can do.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">  I can't seem to find the right girl.   </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's not possible to find the right girl.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">  You may have made the wrong decision. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible that you made the wrong decision.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I understand you might feel frustrated, but you may have made the wrong decision. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Maybe that could help you change your outlook on this.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Expressing an Opinion About Past Events (Simple Past vs Past Perfect)", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Past Perfect tense to identify and talk about an 'earlier past'.<br />  You use the Simple Past to talk about a finished action that happened at a specific time in the past. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " When you are talking about a past event, you can refer to something that happened at an earlier time to that past event by using the <span class=\"underline\">Past Perfect</span> tense.<br /><br />  The structure of the Past Perfect is:<br /><br />  Subject + had + past participle<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">had thought </span>about going to the mall before you called me</span><br /> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">first</span>? I thought about going to the mall.<br /> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">later</span>? You called me.<br /><br />  You use the Past Perfect tense (not Simple Past) when you want to talk about how long something had continued <span class=\"strong\">up to a past moment</span>. <br /> Example:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">I just broke up with a girl I <span class=\"strong\">had met</span> two weeks ago</span>.<br /><br />  You use the Simple Past tense to talk about the action that happened after that prior action in the Past Perfect tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " I thought you had started going out to comic book stores before you met that girl. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What happened? It sounded like a good idea.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to throw in the towel ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to quit or abandon something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Well, I might just throw in the towel. What's the point anyway?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear and use when you are very sad.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dejected ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "terribly sad or depressed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Why do you look so dejected? Is anything wrong?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "despondent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "feeling very sad and depressed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't sound so despondent! Things will change.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "distressing ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "causing someone to feel anxious, stressed or suffering", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can't seem to find the right girl. It's really distressing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hopeless ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "desperate and with no hope ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It might look hopeless now, but there must be something you can do!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "What's the point? ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to express hopelessness and impossibility when facing certain situation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm quitting! What's the point anyway?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "outlook", "type": "name"}, {"content": "perspective you have on something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Maybe that could help you change your outlook on this.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine that you will be joining an online dating service.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a profile. Include a description of yourself (e.g. age, height, etc.).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include a few sentences about yourself and what you are looking for.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include a few sentences about your past experiences.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I describe myself.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe what I am interested in and what interests me.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe my past experiences.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exerci